merged-2026-08-17: PR #44 (`feature/mbco-fixed-branch-ariv`, squash `c748d1b` on dev) —
  medsim_method_mbco_mi() ariv=c("own","fixed") + additive branch diagnostics (indirect_p_fixed,
  branch_mix, p_branch_a, stacked_branch, r4, r4_fixed); .medsim_d4_mbco(fixed_branch=, lls_S=).
  1121 pass / 0 fail. Two /code-review passes: 1 perf fix landed (stacked fit shared), 2 false
  positives verified. goodpractice: 31 package-wide advisories, none PR-introduced. Worktree
  `~/.git-worktrees/medsim/feature-mbco-fixed-branch-ariv` still present (delete when convenient).
  Pre-release adversarial review (3 lenses, 2026-08-17): 1 BLOCKER (Gate A.2 collapse audit
  flagged the new diagnostics), 2 SHOULD-FIX, NITs — all fixed + README/pkgdown refresh in
  PR #45, MERGED (squash 68a2a18). Both worktrees + local/remote branches removed 2026-08-17.
  v0.5.1 RELEASED 2026-08-17 (merge a000108, tag v0.5.1, GitHub release published); dev bumped to
  0.5.1.9000. Missing Effect fixed-branch Hopper re-run is UNBLOCKED (install from r-universe once
  it serves 0.5.1.9000, or `pak::pak("Data-Wise/medsim@v0.5.1")`).
grounded-2026-08-22: Reviewed all open PRs/issues against live GitHub + git state (no drift
  vs memory except one correction below). 0 open PRs (confirmed). 5 open issues found:
  #28, #29, #35, #41, #43. Branch-cleanup entry `(3)` further down in this file (dated
  "[DONE 2026-07-11]") was WRONG — corrected in place; the 7 old feature branches are still
  on origin, unmerged. #35's "blocked-upstream" status (probmed#32, BCa for ward_residual)
  should NOT be read as a stable holding pattern right now: probmed#32 had 3 self-correcting
  comments today (2026-08-22, 00:59/04:34/16:47 UTC), the last a retraction of the prior two,
  pointing to probmed's `docs/specs/REVIEW-2026-08-22-adversarial-refutation.md` (adversarial
  review: the whole Phase-2 bootstrap-replacement approach is refuted by measurement, verdict
  "must not be executed as written"). Do not act on #35 assuming probmed#32 is settled either
  direction — re-check probmed#32 before picking #35 back up.
closed-2026-08-22: **Issue #43 CLOSED** — full fix landed same-day across 3 merged PRs
  (design: `internal/GRILL-medsim-43-parallel-fail-loud-2026-07-31.md`). The held branch
  `claude/pensive-goodall-3e2dfb` was split per its adversarial review rather than merged as-is
  (its bundled parallel re-raise would have converted partial data loss into total loss).
  - PR #47 (`feature/est-error-rename`, squash `523ce14`) — clean half of the split: numeric-kind
    mandatory column `error` → `est_error` (fixes a v0.5.0 regression: the two `error` meanings
    collided and made the documented contract unusable), `_pkgdown.yml:129` fixed, new e2e
    regression test.
  - PR #48 (`feature/combine-gate-fixes`, squash `43946e9`) — Gate A combine hardening:
    schema-vote no longer vetoed by a legit empty chunk, new `partial_chunk` violation, new
    mandatory `dgp_failure` violation. `/code-review` caught a real hard crash
    (`attr(NULL, ...) <- 2L` errors, unlike a no-op `NULL` assignment) in the all-empty-chunks
    edge case — fixed + regression test before merge.
  - PR #49 (`feature/parallel-fail-loud`, squash `8ed4c1f`) — the re-raise done right:
    `medsim_run()`/`medsim_run_chunk()` stop loud with a data-carrying `medsim_run_failure`
    condition on task-level errors (serial + parallel, identical shape), rescuing partial
    results via `e$results` instead of discarding them. Rebased onto #48's squashed tip before
    merge to keep the diff clean (`git rebase --onto`, one commit auto-dropped as
    already-upstream). 12 verification cases per the design doc's §5.
  Net: 1197 pass / 0 fail, R CMD check 0/0/0 on the final merged `dev` state. All 3 worktrees +
  local/remote branches removed. `pensive-goodall-3e2dfb` worktree/branch still needs cleanup
  (superseded by the split — safe to delete, nothing from it was merged directly).
grilled-2026-08-22: All 4 remaining open issues grounded + grilled (7 branches, GD1-GD7).
  Canonical designs — do NOT re-derive from the issue bodies, several of which are wrong:
  `internal/GRILL-medsim-41-chunk-truth-atomic-cache-2026-08-22.md` (implementation-ready),
  `internal/GRILL-medsim-35-gauge-probmed-exposure-2026-08-22.md`,
  `internal/GRILL-medsim-28-cluster-vignette-2026-08-22.md`,
  `internal/GRILL-medsim-29-prod3-adapter-2026-08-22.md` (DEFERRED, no consumer).
  Two NEW correctness findings, both live on dev right now, neither previously filed:
  (a) **truth-cache poisoning** — a failed `truth_function()` warns, then its error sentinel is
      written to the truth cache (`R/runner.R:696-707`) and silently reused by every later run
      with NO warning; folded into #41 as item 4. (b) **gauge/probmed exposure** — probmed's
      per-row IPW weight fix (PR #34) merged to probmed's **dev, not main**; only release v0.3.0
      predates it; medsim's Remotes resolves to main and Suggests has no floor ⇒ every install
      route runs gauge coverage against the buggy estimator (upstream measured ~0.85-0.90 vs
      0.936/0.972 corrected). #35 rescoped around it. Priority order now: #41 → #35 → #28 → (#29 deferred).
